            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A vehicle driver assist system (10; 110) comprising: a housing (12; 112) having a camera (16) mounted therein, the housing (12; 112) having at least one tab (30; 130); and a mounting bracket (14; 114) connectable with the vehicle, the mounting bracket (14; 114) including a channel (20; 120) for receiving the tab (30; 130) on the housing (12; 112), the channel (20; 120) being at least partially defined by an arm (38) extending from a sidewall (18) of the bracket (14; 114), the arm (38) having an end surface (40) and the sidewall (18) having a guide surface (44), the end surface (40) of the arm (38) and the guide surface (44) at least partially defining an insertion opening (42) that faces generally downwardly, the tab (30; 130) on the housing (12; 112) sliding into the channel (20; 120) in the mounting bracket (14; 114) through the insertion opening (42) to connect the housing (12; 112) to the mounting bracket (14; 114), the housing (12; 112) and the tab (30; 130) being pivotal relative to the bracket (14; 114) after the tab (30; 130) has slid into the channel (20; 120), wherein a V-shaped notch (50) in the guide surface (44) is defined by first and second side surfaces (52, 54) of the notch (50) extending at an angle to each other, the first and second side surfaces (52, 54) of the notch (50) extending transverse to the guide surface (44), wherein the tab (30; 130) engages the second notch side surface (54) and a stop surface (68) on the arm (38) when the housing (12; 112) is connected to the bracket (14; 114).</p>
            </abstract>
